      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO PREPOSITIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A preposition is always followed by its object, which must be a noun, pronoun, or gerund in the objective case.",
        "Fixed prepositions following specific verbs, adjectives, and nouns carry the highest weightage in SSC English examinations.",
        "Use 'Between' primarily for two persons or things, and 'Among' for more than two.",
        "'Since' marks a specific point in time, whereas 'For' denotes a duration or period of time.",
        "'In' and 'On' indicate static position, while 'Into' and 'Onto' express movement or continuous direction."
      ],
      "id": "orzlvuo"
    },
